# Coleman Brand — Locked (4778 Required)

**Do not change Coleman colors, materials, shadows, glows, gradients, typography tokens, or glass values** unless the operator’s message includes passcode **`4778`** and clearly describes the brand change.

This applies to the entire Coleman enterprise zone: home, dashboard, intro, stage audio, and shared CSS.

## Source of truth (read-only unless 4778)

| Layer | File | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Root tokens | `app/enterprise/coleman/coleman.css` | Global `--coleman-*` variables, luxury canvas, dashboard shell |
| Home premium | `app/enterprise/coleman/coleman-home-premium.css` | Key orb, nav dock, glass panels, component geometry |
| Home material system | `app/enterprise/coleman/coleman-home-material-system.css` | **Authoritative palette** on `.coleman-reference-home` — 40-step neutral scale + semantic tokens |
| Tailwind bridge | `app/enterprise/coleman/lib/coleman-brand-classes.ts` | Class fragments bound to CSS variables — never hardcode hex in UI |
| Logo | `coleman_logo.png` + `HomeHeader.tsx` | See `coleman-home-logo-locked.mdc` |

## Forbidden without 4778

- Editing HEX/RGBA values in Coleman CSS token blocks
- Replacing CSS variables with inline Tailwind hex (e.g. `text-[#2C2520]`) in Coleman components
- “Refreshing”, “modernizing”, or “matching reference” palette tweaks
- Duplicating conflicting token sets in new files
- Changing `--coleman-font`, tracking, blur, shadow, or glow scales

## Allowed without 4778

- Layout, spacing, component wiring, API logic
- New components that **consume existing** `--coleman-*` / `--cp-*` / material-system variables via `coleman-brand-classes.ts`
- Bug fixes that restore values to the documented spec below (not redesign)

## Canonical home palette (`.coleman-reference-home`)

Use `coleman-home-material-system.css` variables — do not invent alternate creams/taupes.

**Background primary:** `#EEE3D9` (Cream Fog)  
**Text headline:** `#291A11` (Deep Espresso)  
**Text primary:** `#332217` (Espresso)  
**Glass fill:** `rgba(255, 253, 250, 0.29)`  
**Glass border:** `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82)`  
**Accent bronze:** `#785538`  
**Champagne gold:** `#AA8968`  
**Glass blur:** `28px` / deep `36px`

Full 16-section brand spec is maintained in operator docs; agents must read CSS files above before any Coleman UI work.
